 ## Background
-Variational 3D Gaussians were introduced in the paper "latentSplat: Latent 3D Gaussian Splatting for Memory Efficient Novel View Synthesis" by C. Wewer et al. [S1, unofficial]. The method adapts the encoder from pixelSplat [S1, unofficial] to predict variational Gaussian parameters. It is used for novel view synthesis from a small number of reference views, leveraging the efficiency of Gaussian splatting [S1, unofficial].
